#!/bin/sh
# Kissat tuned for unsatisfiable formulas, as CBMC's external SAT solver
# (kani.sh's KANI_SOLVER, bin=kissat-unsat): CBMC runs it on each formula's
# DIMACS file and reads the verdict and the model from its output.
#
# The mode 3 proofs end in one hard unsatisfiable formula. On the four
# longest, run four at a time, it took 448 to 754 s where CBMC's own CaDiCaL
# took 2051 to 4149 s, CaDiCaL called the same way about twice Kissat's
# time, and parallel solvers (plingeling, treengeling, CryptoMiniSat on
# eight threads) longer than CaDiCaL.

if [ "${1:-}" = --version ]; then
    exec kissat --version
fi
exec kissat -q --unsat "$@"
